course: dictionary
lesson: 7158
title: Perfume: a liquid and a smell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A perfume is a liquid with a nice, strong smell that people put on their skin. Read the clues in «Maeve finds Mam's perfume and sprays it on her pillow; it smells like a hug.» Sprays and pillow tell you it is a liquid you can spray.
explain: Perfume can also mean the pleasant smell itself, as in «the perfume of roses». Here nothing is being put on. You are just noticing a smell. Ask yourself: is something being put on, or is something being smelt?
explain: Perfume can be a verb too, meaning to give something a nice smell. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: «Perfume» means a liquid with a nice, strong smell that people put on their skin.
fact: «Perfume» can also mean a pleasant smell, like «the perfume of roses».
fact: Smells spread because tiny particles in the air are always moving, so Mum's perfume reaches your nose from across the room.
fact: Perfume is not for drinking, and it can sting your eyes.
fact: Keepers sometimes spray new smells, such as perfume or spices, in an enclosure, because new smells give animals something to explore.
exercise: «Maeve finds Mam's perfume and sprays it on her pillow.» What is perfume here? | *A liquid with a nice, strong smell that you put on | An empty bottle with no lid | A sweet drink | A soft pillow with a flowery pattern
exercise: «The garden was full of the perfume of roses.» What does perfume mean in this sentence? | A strong wind that blows petals | A liquid you spray on your skin | *A pleasant smell | A bunch of petals to eat
exercise: Why should you never drink perfume? | It tastes too sweet to swallow | It is too cold to drink | It turns into water when it is opened | *It is not for drinking, and it can harm you
test: «Mam wants to perfume the room with flowers.» What does perfume mean here? | To wash your hands | To drink something sweet | *To give something a nice smell | To spray paint on a wall
test: Keepers sometimes spray perfume in an enclosure. Why do they do this? | *New smells give the animals something to explore | To stop the animals from smelling their food | To make the animals fall asleep | To wash the enclosure clean
exam: Which sentence uses perfume to mean a pleasant smell? | Maeve wore perfume to the party | She put perfume on her neck | *The room was full of the perfume of lilies | Mum bought a bottle of perfume
